meta {
  name: Get Product Category by ID
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-categories/6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.n_children: eq 1
}

docs {
  `GET /api/v3/product-categories/{id}` -- fetch a single product category by
  its Mongo ObjectId.

  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account". Fetches the parent
  category created in "Create Product Category.bru" -- `n_children` is `1` after
  the child was created, confirming nesting persisted.

  ## Subpath discovery (Phase 0 technique reused)
  `GET /product-categories/{id}/bogus_xyz` -- 400
  `{"errors":[{"name":"ValueError","description":"Field 'bogus_xyz' not found.
  Available fields: ['id','account_id','name','parent_id','path','slug','order',
  'n_children','created','modified']"}]}`. Unlike products, this raw field list
  matches the spec's `ProductCategoryGetOutputDto` exactly (no undocumented
  internal fields).

  Also confirmed: `GET /product-categories/{child_id}/parent` -- 200, returns
  the expanded parent object (a computed subpath, same as products'
  `categories`/`assets` subpaths -- not in the raw field list above but valid).

  ## Identifier flexibility -- only ObjectId works
  `GET /product-categories/WC%20Test%20Category` (by name instead of ID) --
  **422**, same `ValidationError`/"Id must be of type PydanticObjectId" shape
  as `GET /products/<sku>` in Phase 0. Only the Mongo ObjectId works as
  `{identifier}` on this resource -- `API V3.md`'s identifier flexibility
  claim doesn't hold here.
}

example {
  name: Get Category by ID - Success (200)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-21. Full GET-by-id shape includes account_id, parent_id, and created fields absent from the create response.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-categories/6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b182e
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b182e",
            "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
            "name": "Website Taxonomy",
            "parent_id": null,
            "path": ["Website Taxonomy"],
            "slug": "website-taxonomy",
            "order": 2,
            "n_children": 4,
            "created": "2026-06-22T08:44:08.293000",
            "modified": "2026-06-22T08:44:08.293000"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
